      "side": 1,
      "message": "Feel free to shout at me if I\u0027m wrong, but are we sure this is only supposed to be used by filesystems?\n\nNotably, I see an internal driver that seems to be creating a fence. ...as part of that, it gets some fds. If it encounters an error after getting the fds, it needs to cleanup and it calls `close_fd`. That doesn\u0027t seem wrong, yet this is not a filesystem driver.\n\nNotably, the calls I see being made are:\n* `get_unused_fd_flags()`\n* `anon_inode_getfd()`\n\nMaybe there is a way to reorganize the driver such that there are no calls that could return errors that come after we get the fds, but at the same time it doesn\u0027t seem wrong to be able to error handle this way.",
